  "result": "All 9 tests pass (6 from the original file plus the 3 new stream and count tests).\n\n**Changes in `wire/codec.py`:**\n\n- **Extracted a header parser.** The magic, version, count, and payload-length checks moved out of `decode` into a private helper that returns the count, CRC, and payload. `decode` now calls it and then verifies the checksum, so its behavior is unchanged.\n- **Added `record_count`.** It runs the header parser and returns the count from the header. It still raises `CodecError` on bad magic, wrong version, truncation, or trailing bytes, but it skips the CRC pass and never builds record dicts.\n- **Added `encode_stream`.** It writes the output of `encode` to the file object, so the stream and bytes formats are identical by construction.\n- **Added `decode_stream`.** It reads the file object to the end and hands the bytes to `decode`. A text-mode file object or a read failure raises `CodecError`.\n\nNothing is committed. The `wire/codec.py` file remains the only untracked source change.",
